<section class="honest">

    <div class="container">

        <div class="honest__grid">

            <div class="honest__stat">

                <div class="honest__number">
                    10<span>%</span>
                </div>

                <div class="honest__label">
                    Fixed fee on top of the factory's<br>
                    price — the same rate whether<br>
                    that price is low or high
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="honest__content">

                <div class="honest__eyebrow">
                    <span>07</span>
                    The honest question
                </div>

                <h2 class="honest__title">
                    Aren't you just a middleman<br>
                    with a markup?
                </h2>

                <div class="honest__text">

                    <p>
                        We pass through the factory's price and add a fixed 10% on top of it — not folded into the number. What stays with us is which factory it is: that relationship is built across every client we work with, and it's what keeps the rate down on your next project too, not just this one. We don't gain from a bigger invoice either way — you're free to compare our price against other suppliers, and inflating one quote isn't worth losing a developer we could be working with for the next ten projects. Loyo, PARQ, SWOI, Dodo Pizza and Escape have each brought us more than one project.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <a href="#" class="honest__button">
                    Get a comparative quote for your project
                </a>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>

<style>

